    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Let's say that we have to check if \"level\" is a palindrome or not."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "To solve this problem, let's first think about what arguments should be passed in each recursive call."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Recursive Call"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "First, we will pass \"level\" as an argument to the function. Inside the function, we will check whether the first and the last characters are the same or not."
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "alt": "Check the First and Last Characters",
      "src": "data:image/png;base64,"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "If they are the same, we will call the same function."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "However, this time, we will remove the first and the last characters and pass the resulting substring (\"eve\") as an argument."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Again, we will check if the first and the last characters of \"eve\" are the same or not. If they are the same, the recursion continues."
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "alt": "Check the First and Last Characters in eve",
      "src": "data:image/png;base64,"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "If not, the string is not palindrome, and we will end the recursion."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "content": "How does it work?"
